Upgrade to `@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers` **0.19.0 or later** and set `verbose: false` in your pool config. That version added the option to `cloudflareTest()` and `cloudflarePool()`. It hides verbose workerd runtime logs, such as caught Durable Object RPC errors. It defaults to `true`, so you have to turn it off yourself.

```ts
// vitest.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from "vitest/config";
import { cloudflareTest } from "@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers";

export default defineConfig({
  plugins: [
    cloudflareTest({
      wrangler: { configPath: "./wrangler.jsonc" },
      verbose: false, // silence verbose workerd runtime logs
    }),
  ],
});
```

If you use `cloudflarePool()`, put `verbose: false` in its options instead.

The changelog only shows the `verbose: false` line by itself, not a full config. I added the surrounding `wrangler: { configPath }` structure from the usual setup, so check it against the README for your installed version.

**Other noise you might see:**
- **TLS stack traces:** messages like `disconnected: peer disconnected without gracefully ending TLS session` with a `kj/compat/tls.c++` stack trace come from tests that make real `fetch()` calls. Version 0.19.0 also stops showing these, so upgrading fixes them without any config change.
- **Pool logging:** since 0.14.8 the pool's own logs default to INFO level instead of VERBOSE. If you ever want the detailed output back, for example to see errors from shutting down test workers, run with `NODE_DEBUG=vitest-pool-workers`.

Ludion had no lessons on this, so all of the above comes from the release notes.

Sources:
- [@cloudflare/vitest-pool-workers 0.19.0 release notes](https://newreleases.io/project/github/cloudflare/workers-sdk/release/@cloudflare%2Fvitest-pool-workers@0.19.0)
- [releases.sh: Worker disposal errors no longer fail test runs](https://releases.sh/release/rel_Y9zRdp9--a5wQBMG0Ydpq)
- [releases.sh release notes](https://releases.sh/release/rel_-1tpBtagFwyjpG1nXvGSr)

